<h1 class="h-xl">Editorial <span class="soft">&amp; Systems Governance Rubric</span></h1>
<p class="lead">How I evaluate and hold the line on AI-generated content.</p>
</header>

<section class="wrap rubric" aria-label="The four standards">
<article class="rubric-card">
<span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
<h3>Factual &amp; Contextual Rigor</h3>
<p>Cross-checking outputs against source constraints and knowledge bases to eliminate hallucinations or hollow boilerplate.</p>
</article>
<article class="rubric-card">
<span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
<h3>Structural Integrity</h3>
<p>Ensuring headings, taxonomy, and metadata adhere strictly to style standards and accessibility (WCAG) guidelines.</p>
</article>
<article class="rubric-card">
<span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
<h3>Institutional Tone</h3>
<p>Verifying that voice, pacing, and messaging align with brand guidelines before deployment.</p>
</article>
<article class="rubric-card">
<span class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
<h3>Upstream Iteration</h3>
<p>When an output fails quality control, diagnosing whether the breakdown occurred in prompt instructions, context tokens, or model limitations, and fixing the system upstream rather than editing symptoms downstream.</p>
</article>
</section>

